@page "/Others/Message"
@using de.jweschenfelder.KSFP.Shared.Objects
@using de.jweschenfelder.KSFP.Web.Interfaces.BusinessLogic

<PageTitle>Kerry Shale Fanpage: A mesage for Mr Kerry Shale or Sainou</PageTitle>

<div class="section mt-5 pt-4">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row mb-4 align-items-center">
			<div class="col-lg-4">
				<h2 class="heading">Message<span class="text-primary">.</span> </h2>
			</div>
			<div class="col-lg-4">
				<p class="text-black-50">
					A mesage for Mr Kerry Shale/Sainou.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div>
			<div class="row mb-5 justify-content-between">
				<div class="col-lg-12 text-black-100">
					<p>
						<strong>11th May 2024 - Mr Shale/Sainou will receive a letter from some parcel service.</strong><br /><br />
						Maybe Mr Shale or Sainou or his pal Mr Hare may read this message: Mr Shale is going to receive a package. Unfortunately, I had made a mistake there as I found out meanwhile. 
						It should be a present, but I had not been aware that presents have another amount limit than any bought good when it is in the context of the customs. It means the package is at 
						the customs clearance (DDU) now. That was not my intention, it should not cause any work at all. There are two choices now: <br /><br />
						- Either he accepts the package and unfortunately has to pay a customs duty beforehand. There is <u>some compensation inside that package</u> which can cover those costs, but for that
						he would have to pay the money first to get the package with the compensation inside. But I somehow doubt that he will do that, which I would totally understand, because it needs some 
						trust. <br /><br />
						- Or the second option would be that he simply denies the package and that the customs charges remain unpaid. DHL was requested to send the package back to the sender then. That is also 
						perfectly fine. He shall not worry. <br /><br />
						We will see how it works out, what decision he/Sainou will make. In any case, I am truly sorry for the additional circumstances/additional work/time, it was truly not intended, it 
						should not cause any additional work, and I hope he understands that. I cannot write a direct message/letter to him for that because it would exceed the maximum of possible messages per 
						year. I have learnt from that mistake, it will not happen again. There is a plan B, so please do not worry about it. I understand if he should get confused/irritated when he receives a 
						letter from the customs clearance, especially since he has not requested/ordered something. I am truly for that. I feel guilty. <br /><br />
						Update (11th May 2024): I have contacted the parcel service and have asked them if they allow me to pay the customs charges instead. I am currently awaiting their answer. 
						If the parcel service should not answer or if the parcel service should deny my request, the two options mentioned above become valid. Yes, I am an idiot. I am fully aware of it and I 
						am willing to bear all the consequences. There is no need to tell the tracking number here online, the parcel service will tell him/Sainou the tracking number in a letter. 
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

	</div>
</div>

